    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {"en": "Key dates in Spain"},
      "texto": {
        "en": "- **Nochebuena**, 24 December: many families have a long dinner.\n- **Navidad**, 25 December.\n- **Nochevieja**, 31 December: a common tradition is to eat twelve **uvas**, one with each clock chime at midnight. People often say **¡Feliz año nuevo!**\n- **Reyes**, 6 January: in the Three Kings tradition, children receive presents that day.\n- **Semana Santa** (Holy Week) usually falls in March or April; some places hold processions. **Pascua** means Easter.\n\nFor a birthday: **¡Feliz cumpleaños!** or **¡Felicidades!** There is **una tarta** with **velas**.\n\nThe verbs: **celebrar** el cumpleaños; **invitar a** alguien **a** una fiesta; **regalar** algo **a** alguien (¿qué **le** regalo?); **brindar**: ¡Salud!"
      }
    },
